{%- comment -%}
  Is this collection empty for the market the buyer is in?

  Elder Emo's market catalogs are deliberately narrow: Canada and Australia hold only
  locally printed listings, and the UK holds nothing shipped in from abroad. Collections
  are NOT per-market in Shopify, though. They publish to sales channels only, so every
  collection exists in every market and simply renders with whatever products that
  market can buy. That is why Australia has 26 collection pages that return HTTP 200
  with an empty state, and the UK 21.

  Liquid does see the market, so collection.products_count is already filtered to the
  buyer's catalog. That is the whole mechanism here: nothing needs a hardcoded list, and
  the result follows the catalogs as they change.

  Usage, with `col` set to a collection object:
      {%- render 'market-collection-empty', col: some_collection -%}
  It outputs "true" or "" so it can be captured and tested:
      {%- capture empty -%}{%- render 'market-collection-empty', col: link.object -%}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- unless empty == 'true' -%} ... {%- endunless -%}

  Note all_products_count is NOT used: it ignores the market and would report a
  collection as full when the buyer cannot see any of it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  if col == blank
    echo 'true'
  elsif col.products_count == 0
    echo 'true'
  endif
-%}
